<%# locals: (layer: false) %>
<%# The pages of "Mein Konto", ONE list for the two places that show it:

    - the sidebar of an account page (common/_navigation_account), where it is the
      sidebar's middle;
    - the account layer (common/_account_layer, Belegungstabelle F47), which rises
      over the sidebar of an organisation's page when the reader clicks their name.

    Until 2026-11-12 the second place was a small menu of its own under the name,
    with four of these entries and none of the others (no billing accounts, no API
    tokens, no way to the other organisations): two lists of one area that did not
    agree. A new account page is one entry here and shows in both.

    layer: true adds what only the layer has: the cross that closes it (F20, at the
    end of the label row as F41 has it) and, while the news are in the navigation
    (ApplicationHelper#changelog_in_navigation?), the news of the organisation the
    reader stands in. The label has the form of the sidebar's other labels
    ("PROJEKTE", "VERWALTUNG"). %>
<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 px-3 pb-1.5">
  <p class="font-mono text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-muted"><%= t('navigation.account_section') %></p>
  <% if layer %>
    <button type="button" class="inline-flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-muted transition-colors hover:text-heading"
            title="<%= t('views.common.close') %>" aria-label="<%= t('views.common.close') %>"
            data-action="sidebar-layer#close">
      <i class="bi bi-x-lg text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
  <% end %>
</div>
<ul class="flex flex-col gap-1" data-account-nav-list>
  <%# "Alle Organisationen" (not "wechseln"): from the account section you are not in an
      org context, so the label matches the org switcher menu's cockpit link. %>
  <%= render 'common/navigation_item',
        name: t('navigation.all_organisations'),
        path: select_organisation_path,
        icon: 'bi bi-building',
        active: request.path == select_organisation_path %>

  <%# The inbox above the organisations, only where there is more than one: the
      route sends a person with one organisation to its own inbox. %>
  <% if switcher_organisations(current_user).many? %>
    <%= render 'common/navigation_item',
          name: t('navigation.all_inboxes'),
          path: all_inboxes_path,
          icon: 'bi bi-bell',
          active: request.path == all_inboxes_path %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render 'common/navigation_item',
        name: t('navigation.profile'),
        path: edit_user_registration_path,
        icon: 'bi bi-person-fill',
        active: [edit_user_registration_path, edit_user_registration_password_path, new_account_deletion_path, user_registration_display_path].include?(request.path) %>

  <%# Billing accounts (K1 revised): the area hangs on the account, not on an
      organisation, and the account navigation is the only one that renders without a
      tenant (see layouts/application.html.erb). That way an account owner WITHOUT any
      membership anywhere reaches it too -- that is N1, and the reason the area was
      pulled out of the organisation at all.

      Always visible, not only for people with an account: checking visibility would
      cost one round of Subscriptions::VisibleAccounts on EVERY page that renders this
      list (one role query per organisation of the user), and since the layer that is
      every page of the application. Whoever has none sees the honest empty state,
      just like with the data export. %>
  <%= render 'common/navigation_item',
        name: t('navigation.billing_accounts'),
        path: billing_accounts_path,
        icon: 'bi bi-receipt',
        active: request.path.start_with?('/billing') %>

  <%= render 'common/navigation_item',
        name: t('navigation.data_export'),
        path: user_data_export_path,
        icon: 'bi bi-download',
        active: request.path.start_with?('/user_data_export') %>

  <%# API tokens and preferences are entries of their own since 2026-11-12. Until
      then both hung under a "Präferenzen" group with seven sub-pages. The tokens
      are a function (a list, a create flow), not a setting of how the application
      behaves; the preferences are one page of sections (user_preferences/edit). %>
  <%= render 'common/navigation_item',
        name: t('navigation.settings_api_tokens'),
        path: users_personal_access_tokens_path,
        icon: 'bi bi-key',
        active: request.path.start_with?('/users/personal_access_tokens') %>

  <%= render 'common/navigation_item',
        name: t('navigation.preferences'),
        path: edit_user_preferences_path,
        icon: 'bi bi-person-gear',
        active: request.path.start_with?('/user_preferences') %>

  <% if layer && changelog_in_navigation? && current_organisation.present? %>
    <%= render 'common/navigation_item',
          name: changelog_nav_label(changelog_has_unread?(current_user)),
          path: organisation_changelog_path(organisation_id: current_organisation.id),
          icon: 'bi bi-megaphone' %>
  <% end %>
</ul>
